Divij Vaidya created KAFKA-14615:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Use sizeCompare(Iterable[_]) to compare two iterables
                 Key: KAFKA-14615
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-14615
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Divij Vaidya
             Fix For: 4.0.0


Since Scala 2.12 is being deprecated in 4.x version, we can utilize some im=
proved methods for comparing size of scala collections which were introduce=
d starting 2.13.

This task is to find and replace usage of code paths where we use (Iterable=
A.size =3D=3D IterableB.size) having a complexity of O(IterableA size + Ite=
rableB size) with sizeCompare() method which has a complexity of O(min(Iter=
ableA size, IterableB size))

=C2=A0[1] [https://github.com/scala/scala/pull/6758]
=C2=A0[2] [https://github.com/scala/scala/pull/6950]=C2=A0



